<title>MEXICO: Banco de Mexico to drain 1.816 bln pesos.</title>
<headline>Banco de Mexico to drain 1.816 bln pesos.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-05-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Banco de Mexico sought to drain 1.816 billion pesos from the secondary market on Friday through a combination of three direct sales of paper and three repurchase agreements, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Cetes sales were offered or assigned as follows:</p>
<p>    AMOUNT     TERM	 AVERAGE RATE</p>
<p>    150 million    342 days   22.28 pct</p>
<p>    150 million    181 days</p>
<p>    150 million     90 days</p>
<p>The terms and maturities of the repurchase agreements were offered as follows:</p>
<p>    600 million     31 days</p>
<p>    600 million     17 days</p>
<p>    166 million	3 days</p>
<p>*Amounts in pesos</p>
<p>((--Mexico City Newsroom 525 728-9559))</p>
